  "number": 1115,
  "title": "Where are my fellow Canadians? Novatel Mifi 7000 as a possible CAN Rayhunter?",
  "body": "The Orbic isn't really that cheap when it comes to the CAD. I've seen several Novatel Mifi 7000 devices for sale for $50 CAD. \r\nThe 7000 has the Qualacomm MDM9640 and covers LTE bands B1/B2/B3/B4/B5/B7/B12/B13/B17/B20/B28/B29.\r\n\r\nDoes anyone have one to test? Or has anyone already attempted this?\r\n\r\nI may pick one up the next time I see one locally. I am not much of a code monkey, but I'd certainly give it a try. I'd love to play with a PinePhone, but the Mifi 7000 is  a far cheaper option. ",
